This product includes data derived from third-party corpora, used for
validation and measurement only. None of it is redistributed in the published
package; the fixtures are fetched on demand by `npm run verify:corpus`.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

claude-code-log
  https://github.com/daaain/claude-code-log
  MIT License.
  Used as a pinned public corpus of Claude Code transcripts, for parser
  validation. Commit pinned in scripts/corpus.json.

claude-code-sessions
  https://github.com/frederick-douglas-pearce/claude-code-sessions
  MIT License.
  Used as a pinned public corpus for the same purpose. Commit pinned in
  scripts/corpus.json.

SWE-chat / coding-agent-misalignment
  https://github.com/ND-SaNDwichLAB/coding-agent-misalignment
  Replication package for "How Coding Agents Fail Their Users"
  (arXiv:2605.29442), an analysis of 20,574 real sessions from 1,639
  repositories.
  Used as the labelled set against which this project measures its own judge.
  Its published episode labels are the source of every "silver agreement"
  figure in docs/eval.md. Licence terms are recorded in docs/data-sources.md;
  only permissively-licensed repositories were released upstream.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Every frequency published in docs/ is reproducible from the pinned corpora via
`npm run measure` and `npm run verify:corpus`. The SWE-chat set additionally
requires a Hugging Face login and is ~47 GB — see docs/data-sources.md for what
can and cannot be reproduced without it.
